# "The same is true if the targeted creature's power becomes greater than Old Man of the Sea's power before the ability
# resolves" (its ruling): the target restriction is checked again as the ability resolves (CR 608.2b), and the creature is no
# longer a legal target. Bot1's Old Man targets Bot2's Llanowar Elves; in response Bot2 casts Turn Inside Out on the Elves
# (4/1). The ability does nothing: the Elves stays Bot2's.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Sapphire
Mox Jet
Island
Old Man of the Sea
Island x16

[Bot2 Deck]
Forest
Llanowar Elves
Mox Ruby
Turn Inside Out
Forest x16

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Island.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Island.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Old Man of the Sea.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot2.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Llanowar Elves.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Old Man of the Sea.Activate(Bot2.Battlefield.Llanowar Elves)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Turn Inside Out.Cast(Bot2.Battlefield.Llanowar Elves)
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
? Bot2.Battlefield.Llanowar Elves.Power = 4
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield = Mox Sapphire; Mox Jet; Island; Old Man of the Sea
Bot1.Battlefield.Old Man of the Sea.Tapped = true
Bot2.Battlefield = Forest; Mox Ruby; Llanowar Elves
Stack.Count = 0
